{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/58139-your-thoughts-on-solar-occult","id":58139,"title":"Your Thoughts on Solar Occult","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-26T09:39:04-08:00","id":58139,"title":"Your Thoughts on Solar Occult","content":"You're playing a Solar, and you have dots in Occult. What kind of Charms would you like to get out of this?<br /> <br /> Hard mode: you are not playing a sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T09:57:19-08:00","id":58148,"title":"","content":"Math and Science charms.<br /> <br /> More occulty, I think setting up Wards would be good territory for Occult. I could also see direct Essence manipulation fitting into Occult, but it is hard to think of anything off the top of my head that doesn't fit better under another ability.<br /> <br /> It's really hard to say because most current Lore charms I think are better fits for Occult. I see Occult as the math and hard science ability, as all of the supernatural stuff is just another science in Creation, and Lore is best described as a history and humanities ability.<br /> <br /> So basically, almost everything Lore currently does, but that leaves me with the &quot;Well then what does Solar Lore do?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T09:58:30-08:00","id":58152,"title":"","content":"I have a Night Caste assassin who has Occult favored, and has Spirit-Detecting Glance and Spirit-Cutting Attack (and will get Ghost-Eating Technique), all for the purposes of being able to assassinate spirits.<br /> <br /> I would like to see some Charms that expand on the social side of Occult. Charms that awe spirits, make them like you or fear you, Charms that grant you supernatural prowess of supernatural etiquette. Maybe Charms that grant particular defenses against attacks or social attacks or whatever from spirits.<br /> <br /> Charms that expand on the concept of Spirit-Repelling Diagram would be cool too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T10:48:16-08:00","id":58180,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is possible, but any Occult charms that don't go hand-in-hand with Sorcery would be great. I've always felt like that was the main reason to get Occult, and everything else is just gravy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T10:52:59-08:00","id":58183,"title":"","content":"I actually have a strong opinion about this, so you asked for it!<br /> <br /> Occult in 2e was terrible. It was separated into isolated, distinct systems. 'Mortal Thaumaturgy' was something that Exalted charms just never interacted with ; in fact, the game kinda tried to shame Exalted who would use mortal thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> This was a side effect, of course, of those sections being written by different people who were not coordinating.<br /> <br /> This is lame. An Exalted using Occult is doing the same things a human does, except better. Accordingly, I would like the themes and conventions of the mortal thaumaturgy system... walkaways, prayer strips, etc... reflected in the Exalted systems as well.<br /> <br /> An Exalted with a wide array of Occult charms may not be a 'Sorcerer' in the strictest sense of the word, but they have a firm command of peasant magic and remain exceptionally dangerous and resourceful.<br /> <br /> TLDR; Exalted occult skills and mortal occult skills were isolated in previous editions. Make them the same skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:00:13-08:00","id":58186,"title":"","content":"New charms that don't involve seeing/smelling/hearing/hitting/touching spirits would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:05:24-08:00","id":58189,"title":"","content":"I, too, would like Solar Charms to interact with Thaumaturgy or basically be &quot;Thaumaturgy, but better!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Along those lines, I'd like to see the return of the spirit-warding Charm. For new expansions on that Charm, an inverted ward that <i>traps </i>a spirit in one place, and then a Charm which goes so far as to trap a spirit into a physical object.<br /> <br /> Solars may have to work harder and longer to get there than Sidereals, but having a Charm like Terminal Sanction doesn't seem out of bounds for Solar Occult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:20:56-08:00","id":58197,"title":"","content":"So Sorcery starts at Essence 3 and goes to Essence 5. Why not have Thaumaturgy charms in the Essence 1-3 range?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:39:03-08:00","id":58208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/58139-your-thoughts-on-solar-occult?p=58197#post58197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Sorcery starts at Essence 3 and goes to Essence 5. Why not have Thaumaturgy charms in the Essence 1-3 range?</div> </div> </div> </div>pretty sure sorcery will no longer require essence 3+ in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1174-the-lidless-eye-that-sees","name":"The Lidless Eye That Sees","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1174_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:42:37-08:00","id":58214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/58139-your-thoughts-on-solar-occult?p=58197#post58197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Sorcery starts at Essence 3 and goes to Essence 5. Why not have Thaumaturgy charms in the Essence 1-3 range?</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of the What We Know stuff:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The norm in EX3 is starting at Essence 1 (giving us more of a continuum to build in). The corebook includes a chargen option for more seasoned Solars as well, who have been Exalted for more than a year or perhaps for several years, if you want to start a little ahead of the curve.<br /> <br /> (Before anyone asks, no, sorcerers do not have to wait for Essence 3 to do their thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:48:26-08:00","id":58218,"title":"","content":"This is something I've been pondering lately and the conclusion I reached is pretty straightforward: Sorcery doesn't make you a sage wizardy fellow- being a Twiligh Solar does.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is there for a lot of different things- you can model the powers of all sorts of different characters with it- a holy prophet, a voodoo witch, a spirit caller, an enlightemed strategist and so on. In the end sorcery just makes you a sorcerer and ideally it should, along with Martial Arts and Evocations be able to complimemt any type of a character.<br /> <br /> Now being a Magus... That's a different thing. In Exalted Occult is the propper aplication of rules of the Universe not immediately apparent. It's basically spirit-physics. I could see it as something that when combined with Lore, Investigation, Medicine and Craft would allow you to do stuff that we atribute to sages of legend, like Hermes Trismagistos, King Salomon, or Merlin. I feel like where Lore is &quot;know what&quot;, Occult is &quot;know how&quot;.<br /> <br /> It will, inevitably, always, step on the toes of Lore, but I feel like in the same way nobody should pick Presence without Socialize, or Melee without Martial Arts or Dodge without Athletics, nobody should pick Occult without Lore and vice versa. Ideally, no character should be able to pick just one skill and express their entire character concept with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-26-2014, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T12:17:53-08:00","id":58240,"title":"","content":"Didn't I hear that in 3e Thaumaturgy will no longer be a thing, or at least not something that's in the core?<br /> <br /> Of course, that might just mean that whatever Sorcery looks like at E1, and wielded by mortals, is the new &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot;. There's room in that space to absorb astrology and warding and the rest.<br /> As long as Sorcery is richer than just a gateway Charm and a spell buffet, maybe more like a catch-all term for applied Occult, having the majority of Occult Charms wrap around it isn't necessarily a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T12:21:10-08:00","id":58242,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgy didn't make the core, but <i>Towers of the Mighty</i> will have the rules for Manses, so I'm assuming it'll cover geomancy and any relevant charms as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T13:45:18-08:00","id":58291,"title":"","content":"Is actually the Lore charms I often find myself to want for Occult charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T13:54:01-08:00","id":58293,"title":"","content":"Looking at Solar Occult as it is, I find that it supports two kinds of characters: sorcerers and exorcists.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I think I would enjoy Charms that support, well, <i>occultists</i>. That means Charms that allow you to pronounce curses and blessings, that enhance meditation and allow the creation of <i>tulpa</i>. Possibly some manner of oracular effects, though I'm not sure how to distinguish them from astrological blessings.<br /> A sacrifical Charm would be cool, too: something to give one reason to cut out hearts and raise them to the Sun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/58139-your-thoughts-on-solar-occult?p=58240#post58240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't I hear that in 3e Thaumaturgy will no longer be a thing, or at least not something that's in the core?</div> </div> </div> </div>It won't be in the core, but it's still a thing distinct from sorcery; likewise, sorcery will be recognisable from earlier editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T14:57:46-08:00","id":58334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/58139-your-thoughts-on-solar-occult?p=58291#post58291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is actually the Lore charms I often find myself to want for Occult charms</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them, yeah. The purview of Lore as an ability is barely related to Lore charms. Looking over Solars, I guess charms for teaching, shaping, and mote transfer have value, but it's a shame we don't get charms for *knowing actual lore*. Getting back to Occult, I could see Lore's mote transfer and shaping stuff fitting in better with an ability that deals with magic as a whole and the Fair Folk. Beyond that, 2e's spirit wrangling is a legit use of Occult, though there could be something social to complement all the violent charms. Necromancy needs to have a role, but Solar Occultists should be able to do more than punch ghosts without bringing in other charm sets. And rereading the uses of Occult, I'm struck by the emphasis on knowledge and spirit etiquette and so on that is lacking in the 2e charm trees. In general, I hope 3e brings us more knowledge-y and finesse-ish charms instead of just ways to nuke stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T16:02:16-08:00","id":58380,"title":"","content":"What I'd like to see out of 3rd Ed solar Occult:<br /> <br /> 1) spirit interaction charms like in 2nd ed - because... where else would they go?<br /> <br /> 2) a better ward charm. The 2nd ed. ward charm was kinda weird. I'd prefer one more akin to how a priest might bless an area for a scene or a couple of days... so it doesn't just give the solar an aura of &quot;spirits have to be material around me if they want to be close&quot; - but more of a &quot;At Ess 2 it makes spirits materialize or go away, at Ess 4 it also inflicts aggravated dmg as a terrain hazard on creatures of darkness&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) essence sight, as per usual...<br /> <br /> ...ya that's about it<br /> <br /> regarding thaumaturgy I'd reason that such feats work 'ok' as is - but the whole &quot;you can learn one thauma technique for 1xp&quot; honestly doesn't even seem worth it. Perhaps a lore charm that counts as some flavor of heavenly enlightenment and then BAM you know all the thauma techniques for an entire range of the stuff (art of the dead, spirits, metalurgy, alchemy) at master level - I dunno, but just make it a lot easier and cheaper to get for exalted since essence should mean that you can do all these things so much easier than mortals simply by brute forcing it with your excellencies and a buttload of essence<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T16:07:55-08:00","id":58384,"title":"","content":"Mortal Occultist: I know about other realms, at least heard about them and know what may live there.<br /> Solar Occultist: I am comfortable with other realms and can explore them at my leisure with some preparations available to me.<br /> <br /> Mortal Occultist: I know that the world is not as it seems, that there is a deeper truth to it that I can gain an advantage on and use this for my own purposes.<br /> Solar Occultist: I can catch the mysteries as they flit by, trap the ineffable and pluck the threads of the loom itself if I can silence its guardians for a while.<br /> <br /> Mortal Occultist: When danger arises, I consult my knowledge and ward against dangers seen and unseen. I can aid my people and help preserve us through the dangers to safety.<br /> Solar Occultist: I can spot the approaching danger and counter it, stymie it, confound it, lead it astray into my own trap and thwart it until I can bargain for safe passage and future guarantees of neutrality.<br /> <br /> That's sort of what I'm hoping for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/921-malovich","name":"Malovich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar921_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T17:24:01-08:00","id":58411,"title":"","content":"I've apparently got a fairly different understanding of Lore/Occult than the other people on this thread.<br /> <br /> The way I see the divide between them, past the obvious &quot;Normal Science vs Magic Science&quot; divide, I see Lore as fundamentally being about understanding the rules of how Creation works and Occult being about understanding the rules of how Essence works with a second theme of breaking the rules everyone else plays by.<br /> <br /> With Lore, you've got the charms to teach and educate, but you've also got Charms to move Essence and Willpower around from yourself and into others(knowing how those things move and operate in different vessels), you can assert Creation's laws anywhere, and you have such a deep understanding of how Creation works and how it is put together that given the proper resources(the Wyld) you can make <i>more</i> of it.<br /> <br /> Occult, though, you've got Charms that let you set up a field of Essence that repels the essence of Dematerialized spirits, and you got methods of reaching across the Chasm of the Material to bitchslap them if they get uppity, to detect Essence flows and to analyze them, and to smash apart active workings of Essence. But you've also got Charms that let you kill beings that cannot die, that let you tear power and knowledge that you shouldn't be able to access out of the world, to summon a powerful demon even during times when it should be impossible to summon them, and that you twist up Holy until it would count whoever you happen to be pissed at that day as a Creature of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T20:14:06-08:00","id":58483,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm not sure we should infer the true meaning of Abilities from their Charms. I'd rather see Charms that amplify what the Abilities do. It's counter-intuitive to read an Ability description, decide that your character should or shouldn't be good at that, and then have to separately check out Charms to make sure the stuff you care about is in the same place. <br /> <br /> Here's most of the 2e Lore write up:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Characters with the Lore Ability have some knowledge of current events, history, geography and the customs of other lands, as well as the magical secrets of First Age technology.... <br /> Trait Effects: Someone with Lore 1 is literate and can find most large nations on a map of Creation. Someone with Lore 3 knows details of the customs of lands thousands of miles away and can help operate, maintain and service many First Age devices. Someone with Lore 5 knows details of the history of the Shogunate as well as the truth about the mysterious Dragon Kings. In addition, she can maintain and repair the most complex First Age devices, including warstriders. </div> </div> </div>Very little of that is reflected in the Charm set. All the customs/etiquette stuff gets eaten by social Charm sets and the repair stuff ends up with Craft. Maybe knowledge of history and current events is too hard to translate into worthwhile charms? Still, I don't get mote transfer or fighting the Wyld as elements of Lore. Now here's Occult:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Ability represents a character\u2019s knowledge of and familiarity with all forms of magic, ranging from the Charms of the Exalted to the minor but ubiquitous workings of mortal thaumaturgy. In addition, it also covers familiarity with all manner of supernatural creatures, including ghosts, gods, elementals and the Fair Folk. Characters who are skilled in Occult know both the capabilities of such creatures and how to petition or appease them. </div> </div> </div>Again, I think charms should be amplifying what we see here, not going in a new direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T06:17:44-08:00","id":58659,"title":"","content":"I'd like a Solar occultist to be like a luminary geomancer, great exorcist, or Taoist/Buddhist sage like from Japanese and Chinese folklore. The sort of person the Emperor calls in when elementals keep manifesting at unusually high rates in the nation's capitol, or when a demon has possessed his firstborn child and none of the lesser spiritualists seem able to dislodge it. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_(son_of_Jacob)#Joseph_in_prison\" target=\"_blank\">The sort of person that Pharaoh calls to interpret his strange dreams</a>!<br /> <br /> Heaven and Earth should move in harmony with a Solar occultist, and the hidden currents of the world should be apparent to them. Solar occultists should be able to expel spirits possessing/haunting a person, object, or location with the power of their concentrated holiness, whether through masterful and efficacious ritual at lower levels or simply with a word shouted like thunder at higher levels. A Solar occultist should be able to, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunstan#Legacy\" target=\"_blank\">when the Devil appears to tempt her, take it by the nose with her furnace tongs and hammer it silly</a>, then lock it in a (fragile, easily opened) box for a few centuries.<br /> <br /> Occult-focused Solars should have a refined understanding of demesnes, manses, and dragon lines, not merely the currents of the Terrestrial energies but the strange death-haunted vales or the places holy to the Sun, Moon, and Stars; they should be able to use this understanding to make recommendations about how to effectively cope with or modify an area's geomancy - landscaping and architectural changes, for example, or ritual festivals that vent accumulated Essence-pressure, or changing governmental policies that grate on the sensibilities of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Correspondingly, communication and interaction with spirits is obviously a must, although spirit-communication Charms might also be available through Performance, Linguistics, Awareness, and so on. This could be expanded even beyond the simple &quot;sense their presence/perceive them/touch them&quot; progression of 2E - a Solar occultist might take a Charm that allows spirits to pass them messages in their dreams, even if the spirit couldn't normally speak without manifesting or send dreams to people. If there's any space in Solar themes for them to get prophetic or clairvoyant dreams or visions, Occult is where I'd want to put it; by the same token, Solars attuned to the subtle currents of Creation should be able to sense the approach or attention of powerful entities or forces, such as typhoons or a Dusk Caste.<br /> <br /> A Charm or Charms to resist possession and/or illusions seems like a must, although that might better belong in Integrity.<br /> <br /> That's my two cents, anyway ^^;. Playing characters like that (who are pretty common in media) wasn't really viable in 2E, sadly, and it seems like something that could enrich a game. Obviously, taking Occult isn't going to make you an omnicompetent toolbox just because there's spirits involved - being able to touch them won't do you a lot of good if you don't have the fighty Charms to wrestle with them, nor will being able to speak to them do you much good if you don't have the social mojo to bargain with them. But I think there's some space that other Abilities don't already fill in which Occult could have some fun, flavorful, and useful effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T09:18:51-08:00","id":58774,"title":"","content":"I'd also think it was cool if a Solar occultist could, sort of drawing on how the Sun's Exigence empowers lesser gods to select Chosen, send a surge of Essence to an object's least god, temporarily animating the object as a loyal <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsukumogami\" target=\"_blank\">tsukumogami</a> for use as a general-purpose minion. I have an odd predilection for inanimate-objects-minion-commander characters - as you can imagine, I really enjoyed Shaman King. That's far from central to the Solar Occult concept I've espoused above, though, and more a matter of individual preference.<br /> <br /> Drawing further inspiration from Shaman King: there might exist a Solar Occult Charm or tree of Charms that draws on the legacy of the Dragon King <i>olchilike</i>, warriors possessed by the spirits of the gods to serve as champions, that allows a Solar and a spirit riding the Solar to work together at greater efficiency than the spirit's own Charms would otherwise allow. It could be counterbalanced by making the Solar a more attractive target for unwilling possession, of course... Similar effects might grant the Solar additional benefit from being blessed by a spirit or acting as a champion on behalf of a spirit or group of spirits, mechanics obviously subject to whatever form such blessings end up taking. That would tie in neatly with the Usurpation, too - while the Solars ruled with the favor of Heaven and Earth and acted to preserve the good order of the world, they were invincible, but when the spirits withdrew their favor in fear of their might or displeasure at their hubris, the bright kings fell to the Terrestrials' blades.<br /> <br /> Sort of like Craft and the social Abilities, I feel that Occult will be most compelling if 3E gives it a strong mechanical foundation to interact with, as the combat Abilities have historically benefited from. Fun, flavorful, and well-designed thaumaturgy (but not too crunchy and fiddly, because that way lies broken combos and system bloat) will work wonders, and take a lot of the weight of bearing the entire conceptual load of the exorcist-spiritualist-geomancer-psychic spectrum off of Occult Charms for all splats. If spirit mechanics can be designed so that they integrate well with those aspects of the thaumaturgy system that mess with spirits, even better! Although I believe the devs have stated that they were moving away from a unified toolbox-style &quot;spirit Charmset&quot;, so that may be a less daunting task than it appears if each spirit can be tailored as appropriate.<br /> <br /> An Occult-focused Martial Arts Style based around &quot;blasto wizard&quot;-style Essence manipulation, or around the sort of feats attributed to Buddhist and Daoist sages, could be cool, if done properly. Mortal Techniques might let you do things like boil water with your qi or knock objects over from across a room without touching them; with active Essence you could graduate to things like energy shields, levitation, tagging people or an area with sourceless phosphorescence that makes sneaking about unseen difficult, or shooting blasts of energy from your palms or eyes or nose or something like that. That all might be more appropriate to render as She Who Lives In Her Name native charms, though, or not be flavor-appropriate for the setting at all.<br /> <br /> If only there was a way to make multiple Charms or abilities that gave you an energy blast not redundant, or somehow work with each other harmoniously! :T<br /> <br /> <b>N.B. </b>I'm less excited about/committed to all of these ideas than I am to the ones in my previous post, so if (like Kukla) you have endorsed said post please do not feel that your words are being stretched to cover this one as well. This is moving more into the realm of &quot;what I think would be cool&quot; than it is &quot;what would definitely work for everyone.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T10:21:24-08:00","id":58840,"title":"","content":"I am totally in favour of glorious kung fu medium Charms and commune-with-the-least-gods Charms.<br /> Not so much the Martial Art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T11:13:59-08:00","id":58912,"title":"","content":"If the devs refuse to make an Occult-based martial artist possible I'll just have to make it myself. No way am I going through another edition without ever getting to play Solar Negi Springfield.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T12:06:21-08:00","id":58979,"title":"","content":"I am a student of philosophy and I can say one thing- Logic is a strange creature. The knowledge about the rules themselves is pretty straightforward, but curiously knowing the rules is not enough, it requires skillful application of them to solve complex problems and establish a really sound reasoning. I say it not without a certain disdain, but it requires certain talent, skill that can be aquired with time, but which isn't inherent with knowing the rules.<br /> <br /> That's how I'd like to see Occult realised- as a skillful application of knowledge you have about the rules underlying the World. Just knowing the rules themselves can be a number a different abilites, including but not limited to: Lore, Medicine, Craft, Socialize and so on. But Occult is the way you're applying rules that you know- how to apply specific rites of purifaction, how to write a specific prayer, how to forsee the next Lunar/Solar eclipse, how to set an apropriate date for a ritual and so on and so on.<br /> <br /> And so I'd like to see Solar charms expand on it- allowing for fast and accurate calculations about astronomical events, hastening the process of finding the natural veins of Essence, making alchemy and desigining rituals, creating wards. Of course that's on top of what's already there- being able to phsycially interact with spirits and seeing patterns of Essence.<br /> <br /> At least that's what I'd like to see. Also- Golden Demon, you're a credit to the society. Wakfu english dub man, that's amazing. And I think I know the comic that avatar pic comes from- it was awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-27-2014, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:29:09-08:00","id":80604,"title":"","content":"Let's revive this here thread, and turn it into one of those &quot;give the devs ideas&quot; threads.<br /> Which is what it was always intended to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:59:10-08:00","id":80626,"title":"","content":"My character in the Gunstar Autochthonia game I'm in is invested in Occult not for sorcery, but so she knows exactly what to break and how to do it to fuck up the Primordials forces' days. I like it as a thing Occult can do, especially without sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T18:20:12-08:00","id":80675,"title":"","content":"Occult was always very ill defined, and I am hoping that they've tightened up its thesis in 3e, but in the meantime it's hard to say what I want out of Occult because it's hard to say what Occult is or should be. That said, I think the 2e Occult tree was up there with Medicine in covering its bases well, but feeling a lot like a blandly mechanistic swiss army knife. I am hoping to get at least one cascade that is about being an eerie transcendent mystic instead of about solving all the problems associated with spirits and magic, one by one, in the most straightforward way possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T18:45:31-08:00","id":80691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/58139-your-thoughts-on-solar-occult#post58139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're playing a Solar, and you have dots in Occult. What kind of Charms would you like to get out of this?<br /> <br /> Hard mode: you are not playing a sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly I would like to get Charms that let me punch gods in the face.<br /> <br /> I play a Dawn Caste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/994-heroicantagonist","name":"heroicantagonist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar994_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T23:14:51-08:00","id":80829,"title":"","content":"First of all the Devs need to discriminate what is Occult and what is Lore.<br /> <br /> Since Occult seems to encircle the hard sciences, I'd like to see math and physics charms. I'd also like to see charms that deal with the ecology of the little gods. Ask/command Maxwel's friction deamons to be more rough / more smooth, dictate how hot a fire daemon should be, or tell gravity deamons to &quot;ignore me for just a moment.&quot; If these sound like Fate Errors... that's because they are essentially controlled minor Fate Errors.<br /> <br /> I'd like charms that reference old(er) theories / schools of thought. Luminifiours Aether, Steady State Theory, Friction Daemons, Etc. If a theory was popular in the 17-1800's, or was debunked by General Relitivity/Quantum Theroy then it happens to work in Creation. Just to underscore how the very physics of Creation is different from Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T23:34:47-08:00","id":80838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wingnut2292</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/58139-your-thoughts-on-solar-occult?p=80829#post80829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all the Devs need to discriminate what is Occult and what is Lore.<br /> <br /> Since Occult seems to encircle the hard sciences, I'd like to see math and physics charms. I'd also like to see charms that deal with the ecology of the little gods. Ask/command Maxwel's friction deamons to be more rough / more smooth, dictate how hot a fire daemon should be, or tell gravity deamons to &quot;ignore me for just a moment.&quot; If these sound like Fate Errors... that's because they are essentially controlled minor Fate Errors.<br /> <br /> I'd like charms that reference old(er) theories / schools of thought. Luminifiours Aether, Steady State Theory, Friction Daemons, Etc. If a theory was popular in the 17-1800's, or was debunked by General Relitivity/Quantum Theroy then it happens to work in Creation. Just to underscore how the very physics of Creation is different from Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that we're going to see much more of &quot;least gods work the physics of the setting&quot;, seeing as how that's supposed to be what the Loom of Fate does. Getting least gods to do things has really been a Sidereal thing, too. As for &quot;welcome all archaic and discredited material&quot;, that's getting a bit too much Ascension in here, and also is being different just to be different, when a number of things tend to operate with the same parameters and with familiarity to what happens in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T04:51:09-08:00","id":80962,"title":"","content":"An idea I had reading this thread:<br /> <br /> Extruded Essence Marker<br /> Simple, 2m (+1m per day), Occult 2, Essence 2<br /> Duration: One day<br /> The key to the study of the occult is the understanding of the nature of Essence. This Charm is an extension of the Solar's natural ability to channel the Sun's essence. Cupping her hand, she coheres a few motes of her Essence into a glowing liquid form. This casts bright light like an anima at the Bonfire level. She may use this extruded Essence like ink or paint, writing glowing messages or lighting dark passages. She may also with a successful (Dexterity+Thrown) attack, with an accuracy of +0, paint an enemy in combat. This makes stealth impossible as though the target has an anima burning at bonfire levels. The congealed Essence can be removed, but it requires a significant amount of time and attention to scrub it off. The Solar may dismiss the glowing Essence at will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/69-fortycakes","name":"fortyCakes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar69_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:17:12-08:00","id":81901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wingnut2292</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/58139-your-thoughts-on-solar-occult?p=80829#post80829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Occult seems to encircle the hard sciences, I'd like to see math and physics charms.</div> </div> </div> </div> These seem like fine ideas, but for Lore.<br /> <br /> I actually am relatively happy with the current Occult tree. The Lore tree, however, seems full of stuff that should be sent over to Occult. Chaos-Repelling Pattern, Essence-Lending Method, Wyld-Shaping Technique, Order-Affirming Blow... this is all magic stuff. And once you've sent that over to Occult, then Occult has a lot in it, and all Lore has left is the teaching charm. So Occult doesn't really need new stuff, it's Lore that does. Though, as people have said with the warding charm, obviously some charms can be made better or different. But interacting with magic and dealing with spirits, which is the current tree, do seem like the core points of Occult (and its odd that seeing magic is in Occult, while moving magic is in Lore). And obviously there's more you can do for interacting with spirits.<br /> I've always thought that, for Solars, it'd make sense to have social charms that exploit the Creation-Ruling Mandate on a metaphysical level to affect Gods and Elementals.<br /> <br /> I don't like this idea of Occult and Lore covering different types of science. No, Occult is <i>Occult</i>. It's not important to come up with some sort of scientific system for splitting them up. Is it something to do with real learning in the real world? Lore. Is it something magic? Occult. The only magical-type stuff I might be tempted to have in Lore is Alchemy, because it's kind of a primitive kind of Chemistry with a lot of misunderstandings.<br /> The themes that jump out at players are much more important for a fantasy game than making a well thought-out logical basis that people within a magical world (where learning about how the world works means learning about magic) might come up with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T12:26:41-08:00","id":82222,"title":"","content":"I can understand the appeal for the see/kill dematerialized spirits to be under the same tree, but those effects seem like side notes on artifacts or something that could/should fall under awareness and melee/brawl respectively. What I'd like Occult to be able to do would involve countering/enhancing spirit-based (god, elemental, demon, etc.) magic. Perhaps even a branch for each type of being that enhances your ability to interact within those realms while the more broad effects fall under actual sorcery. Speaking of sorcery, I would also like to see each exalted splat be able to make their flavor of sorcery unique through their charms. As an example, Lunars could possibly get more motes or will to feed their casting by moonlight, Sidereals speed the execution of rituals related to astrology or divination, Solars get more force or solidity in their spells in sunlight, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T02:15:26-08:00","id":82565,"title":"","content":"Well, what they've said about 3rd ed sorcery included talking about different &quot;initiation charms&quot; you can get, such as Wyld Initiation, some Solar Initiation charms, and so on. Possibly Necromancy is one. It's apparently a type of sorcery that produces some unique spells.<br /> So that would imply something like the Yozi Initiation charms of 2nd ed, which change your sorcery slightly. And since Solar Initiation was mentioned specifically, that might imply there's a Lunar initiation, etc. So I think you might get your wish!<br /> <br /> On the Occult, I can see some logic behind putting seeing spirits in awareness, punching them with other combat charms, etc, but it seems more appropriate for the Exorcist, the Cultist, the Priest or the Shaman to be able to see and punch spirits than the gladiator, the eagle-eyed archer, the canny thief, etc. So in terms of character building, I think they fit better in Occult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T07:43:13-08:00","id":82622,"title":"","content":"I want charms that mimic sorcery on a smaller and more personal scale","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T07:46:52-08:00","id":82628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/58139-your-thoughts-on-solar-occult?p=82565#post82565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Occult, I can see some logic behind putting seeing spirits in awareness, punching them with other combat charms, etc, but it seems more appropriate for the Exorcist, the Cultist, the Priest or the Shaman to be able to see and punch spirits than the gladiator, the eagle-eyed archer, the canny thief, etc. So in terms of character building, I think they fit better in Occult.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would place exorcism effects more in the performance tree, just like exorcism was performance based in 2e's if the 6-7pt version of the priest merit came into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T08:01:32-08:00","id":82633,"title":"","content":"Eh, regardless of the badly written merits in Scroll of Heroes, exorcism ought to be part of Occult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T06:08:37-08:00","id":83129,"title":"","content":"The classic tree of See Spirit, Hit Spirit, Kill Spirit should still be there (but maybe condensed or modified somehow), and the off shoots of Force Spirit Material (but perhaps made stronger by not giving them the option of automatically turning away) and See Essence both also seem to belong. I would love to see some Charms like:<br /> <b>Spirit Binding Trap</b>: Like Spirit Repelling Diagram, but instead of forcing them away trapping them within an area for a time.<br /> <b>Altering the Keys</b>: A charm that gives you several options for modifying the circles used for summoning Demons or Elementals. Examples are summoning two of the same demon (only usable on First Circle), granting that demon a mutation or unique ability when binding it for a task so that it is better suited to what you want, or forcing a specific intimacy onto it. You get one version when you purchase the Charm and can purchase the others at a reduced xp cost. Various options could also have varying Essence, XP and Occult ratings.<br /> <b>Sacrifice of Worth: </b>In both editions an unexploited use, at least in the Charm set, for the Occult ability was that it gave you the knowledge how to interact with spirits or all stripes. This Charm enhances that knowledge by enhancing the ritualistic giving of a gift such that it becomes more appealing and the Spirit becomes more likely to give his favor. For this Charm to work an elaborate ceremony, speech, or gift creation process should probably be necessary. Also of note is that this Charm does not help the Solar perform the ritual, let him know how to, or tell him what the Spirit likes. The Solar must know those things already.<br /> <br /> I would also love to see other Charms that enhance both Thaumaturgy and Sorcery, as both are flavor wise extremely distinct in my mind and mechanical support should be given to characters who want to pursue one or both of those paths. I want an ability that lets the Solar understand the magical make up of his world and Charms that let him exploit, alter, enhance or destroy it. A Solar with a large repertoire of Occult Charms should be feared and sought after by all manner or Gods, Demons, Humans and Exalt, because they know things that others do not and can do things that seemingly defy the very nature of reason. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":777,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/777-bronze-tiger","user":"Bronze Tiger","date":". 03-03-2014, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/777-bronze-tiger","name":"Bronze Tiger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}